 35CL c  1991Li12: The bremsstrahlung photon beam was produced by focusing a    
 35CL2c  4.1-MeV electron beam onto a radiator target of a gold disc on a water 
 35CL3c  cooled copper at the bremstrahlung facility at the Stuttgart Dynamitron
 35CL4c  Accelerator. The nuclear resonance fluorescence targets contain        
 35CL5c  {+35}Cl. |g rays were detected using 3 Ge detectors. Measured E|g,     
 35CL6c  |I|g. Deduced |s of photon scattering.                                 
 35CL c  1966Ho02: E{-|g}=1.0-1.3 MeV |g-rays from bremstrahlung production by  
 35CL2c  electrons impinging on a thin layer of lead with the electrons from the
 35CL3c  1.4 MeV pressurized cascade electron accelerator of the Diamond        
 35CL4c  Research Laboratory in Johannesburg. Targets of C{-2}Cl{-6}. A 7.6-cm  
 35CL5c  by 7.6-cm NaI crystal. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced half-life for the    
 35CL6c  level of 1220 keV by the resonance scattering of photons.              
